t;td colspan="2" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;115,036&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;114,140&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-top:1pt solid #000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Less accumulated depreciation:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;(4,566)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="2" style="padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;(3,497)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Property, plant and equipment, net&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;110,470&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:bottom"/&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0 2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;$&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;110,643&#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td style="border-bottom:1pt solid #000000;border-top:1pt solid #000000;padding:2px 1pt 2px 0;text-align:right;vertical-align:top"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;2.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company entered into an O&amp;amp;M Agreement and an Administrative Services Agreement ("ASA") with subsidiaries of NEER whereby the Company pays a certain annual fee plus actual costs incurred in connection with O&amp;amp;M and administrative services performed under these agreements. The Projects also entered into a Broker Agreement ("QSE") whereby a wholly-owned subsidiary of NEER acts as a broker for the Projects to sell the energy produced in exchange for a fixed fee that escalates annually.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has various payable amounts due to other related parties for equipment parts, utilities, advertising, payroll, and management fees. The amounts due to and due from related parties are generally non-interest bearing, do not have any stated terms, and are generally paid within 30 days.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;3.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;OPERATING REVENUES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Revenue Recognition - Revenue is recognized when control of the promised goods or services is transferred to customers at an amount that reflects the consideration to which the entity expects to be entitled in exchange for those goods and services.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's operating revenues are generated primarily from a non-affiliated party (the "power purchaser") under the terms of the Power Purchase Agreement ("PPA"). Revenue is recognized as energy is delivered based on rates stipulated in the PPA. The Company believes that the obligation to deliver energy is satisfied over time as the customer simultaneously receives and consumes benefits provided by the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;A PPA with a non-affiliated power purchaser stipulates the prices and terms upon which the project sells power. This arrangement is summarized below:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:98.958%"&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:35.591%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.401%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:26.418%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.401%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:8.072%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.401%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:10.328%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.401%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:1.0%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:11.687%"/&gt;&lt;td style="width:0.1%"/&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Project&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Counterparty&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Term in years&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Expiration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-right:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Price per MWh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:112%"&gt;Harmony Solar II, LLC&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Orlando Utilities Commission&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;20&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:right"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Calibri Light',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;2043&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:0 1pt"/&gt;&lt;td colspan="3" style="background-color:#f2f2f2;border-bottom:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-left:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-right:1pt solid #bfbfbf;border-top:1pt solid #bfbfbf;padding:2px 1pt;text-align:left;vertical-align:top"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;33.76&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;4.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;COMMITMENTS AND CONTINGENCIES&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company has no outstanding commitments and contingencies other than those occurring from normal operations which are properly reflected as liabilities within the project financials.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:700;line-height:120%"&gt;5.&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;SUBSEQUENT EVENTS&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style="text-align:justify"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;The Company's management has evaluated the recognition and disclosure of subsequent events for its March 31, 2026 financial statements through May&#160;27, 2026, noting no additional disclosures are required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfImportantDisclosuresRegardingTheFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
